# Code standards

## File size limit

- **No component or screen file may exceed 350 lines of code.**
- If a file grows beyond 350 lines, split it by:
  - Moving screen-specific UI into a subfolder (e.g. `screens/Splash/SplashLetter.tsx`).
  - Extracting styles into a `*.styles.ts` file.
  - Extracting constants into a `constants.ts` file.
  - Extracting subcomponents into their own files in the same feature folder.

## Screens folder structure

Each screen lives in its own folder under `src/screens/`:

```
screens/
├── Splash/
│   ├── SplashScreen.tsx    # Main screen component
│   ├── SplashLetter.tsx    # Screen-specific subcomponents
│   ├── splashScreen.styles.ts
│   ├── constants.ts        # Screen-specific constants
│   └── index.ts            # export { SplashScreen }
├── Home/
│   ├── HomeScreen.tsx
│   └── index.ts
├── Login/
│   ├── LoginScreen.tsx
│   └── index.ts
└── index.ts                # Re-export all screens
```

- One folder per screen; screen name in PascalCase (e.g. `Splash`, `Home`).
- Export the main screen from the folder’s `index.ts`; root `screens/index.ts` re-exports for navigation.
